  "boundaries": [
    "Original arithmetic witnesses call exact original peer split code and fail downstream representability assertions. They do not execute original casts/scaler or construct a network/channel using those values.",
    "Six final controls inspect real small configuration objects and call the public invalid constructor without a Tokio runtime; early error is verified. No enormous channel allocation, live startup or resource exhaustion test.",
    "Numeric maxima are representational, not practical operating recommendations. 32-bit conditional source reviewed; no 32-bit target compiled.",
    "Execution constructor preflight precedes its NAT/network work. Node runtime reaches that constructor after shared setup, then logs and exits1 on error.",
    "Existing live request/response contents, protocol limits, same-session accounting, provider API and cache ownership are unchanged. No per-request or ingestion work added.",
    "Current per-message, per-operation, queue and cache controls are distinct from global process memory admission. No RSS, throughput, per-node absolute byte bound or instant cancellation guarantee inferred.",
    "Canceled already-admitted requests and owned provider copies are documented existing lifetimes; optional early skip/cursor-aware API changes are not implemented without a demonstrated need.",
    "All vendor sources unchanged from PR226. Local standalone gossip expiry rerun omitted for this unrelated fix; exact-source local/platform controls are recorded in PR226 and current Linux/macOS CI runs them again.",
    "No benchmark, live sync, remote host, production-data change, deployment or dependency update. Query policy, automatic verified repair and integrated acceptance remain separate."
  ]
